{%- comment -%}
  Urgency treatment for the hero SKU only.

  The 3-Month Supply is the product we buy cold traffic for, so its page is allowed to
  push harder than the rest of the catalogue: a red "limited time" badge and a red sale
  price instead of the house navy. Every other product page is untouched.

  ⚠️ The rest of the store deliberately frames the 18% as a FOUNDING COHORT, not a sale,
  precisely so nobody learns to wait for the next discount (PRICING.md, and the reason the
  old countdown timer was deleted). "Limited time" pulls the other way. It is honest only
  for as long as the founding price really is going to end, so the supporting line names
  the thing that actually ends it: the first 500 customers.

  ⚠️ NO <script> TAGS IN HERE. This snippet is rendered through a `custom_liquid` block
  setting, and Shopify does not execute script tags inside those - the whole block comes
  out empty, silently. The red price is done in CSS with :has(), and anything that needs
  real JavaScript lives in assets/mb-pdp-recipe.js.

  Rendered as a custom_liquid block after `price` in templates/product.json.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if product.handle == 'meow-belle-3-month-supply' -%}
  <div class="mb-urgency">
    <span class="mb-urgency__pill">Limited time</span>
    <span class="mb-urgency__note">
      Founding price, for the first <b>500</b> cat parents only. It does not come back.
    </span>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
